    {"problem": "Your Westdale home has radiators, and every installer says add ducts first", "solution": "You don't need ducts. A multi-zone ductless heat pump runs up to five wall or ceiling heads off one outdoor unit, each room on its own remote. The boiler stays for the coldest stretch of January, and the heat pump carries cooling, the shoulder seasons and most of the winter."},
